From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:14:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(scmi): accept CLOCK_CONFIG_SET from clock protocol v1/v2
 agents

Agents that implement SCMI clock protocol v1 or v2 send CLOCK_CONFIG_SET
with only clock_id and attributes (8 bytes); the extended_config_val
field was added in v3. The server advertises v3 but answered the shorter
message with PROTOCOL_ERROR, so such agents cannot enable any clock.

Linux before 6.7 is such an agent: on RK3568 with the Rockchip 6.1
kernel the NPU and GPU failed to probe with 'Failed to prepare clk
scmi_clk: -71'.

Accept both lengths. With the short form, an extended config type cannot
be applied and is rejected as invalid.

Signed-off-by: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
---
 drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c b/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
index 1e5d7776e..78f3b4016 100644
--- a/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
+++ b/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2019-2020, Linaro Limited
  */
 #include <cdefs.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
 #include <drivers/scmi-msg.h>
@@ -476,7 +477,13 @@ static void scmi_clock_config_set(struct scmi_msg *msg)
 	unsigned int clock_id = 0U;
 	uint8_t extended_config_type = 0U;
 
-	if (msg->in_size != sizeof(*in_args)) {
+	/*
+	 * Agents that implement clock protocol v1/v2 send this message without
+	 * extended_config_val (8 bytes instead of 12); accept both.
+	 */
+	if ((msg->in_size != sizeof(*in_args)) &&
+	    (msg->in_size != offsetof(struct scmi_clock_config_set_a2p,
+				      extended_config_val))) {
 		scmi_status_response(msg, SCMI_PROTOCOL_ERROR);
 		return;
 	}
@@ -492,6 +499,12 @@ static void scmi_clock_config_set(struct scmi_msg *msg)
 
 	extended_config_type = in_args->attributes & SCMI_CLOCK_EXTENDED_CONFIG_SET_TYPE_MASK;
 
+	/* The short (v1/v2) message has no extended_config_val to apply. */
+	if ((extended_config_type != 0U) && (msg->in_size != sizeof(*in_args))) {
+		scmi_status_response(msg, SCMI_INVALID_PARAMETERS);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if ((extended_config_type == 0U)
 	    && (enable == SCMI_CLOCK_CONFIG_SET_UNCHANGED_STATE)) {
 		scmi_status_response(msg, SCMI_INVALID_PARAMETERS);
